# Optional. The regional Agility Management API this app should call.
#
# Normally the app detects this from the manager that embeds it (document.referrer),
# which is what you want in production - an instance in Canada must not be reached
# through the US host. Set this only for local development, where the app may be
# opened directly rather than through the CMS.
#
# https://mgmt.aglty.io       US (default)
# https://mgmt-dev.aglty.io   dev / QA
# https://mgmt-ca.aglty.io    Canada
# https://mgmt-eu.aglty.io    Europe
# https://mgmt-aus.aglty.io   Australia
# https://mgmt-usa2.aglty.io  US 2
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_AGILITY_MGMT_API_URL=https://mgmt-dev.aglty.io

# Where focus keyphrases are stored: Upstash Redis via the Vercel Marketplace.
# Installing the "Upstash for Redis" integration on the Vercel project sets
# KV_REST_API_URL / KV_REST_API_TOKEN automatically; a database created in
# Upstash's own console gives UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL / _TOKEN. Either pair works.
# With neither set, development holds keyphrases in memory (lost on restart);
# production refuses to save at all and tells the editor so.
#
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=https://xxxx.upstash.io
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=xxxx
